WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.170
It's Sunday, November 22, and this is the Transhuman Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.990
Here are the last 24 hours in transhumanism, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.800
It checks out!

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.990
The week's biggest story: computer checkers confirm the Riemann proof Claude helped write.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:27.000
And in a Neuralink video, a paralysed man plays GTA 6 with his mind.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.520
In Toronto,

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.770
a new test found 'brain-like' vision AI works quite differently inside.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:39.650
At Harvard,

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:45.840
faster nanoscale imaging of mouse brain wiring suggests neurons nibble on their neighbours.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.910
Electrodes in 87 people's brains revealed a pos

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:51.880
sible route for expectations to dial pain down.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.960
And Amazon says hackers' AI agents found a new

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:59.080
hole in medical imaging software in 11 minutes.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.420
On to longevity. Closer to home,

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:06.800
Monash found a rogue gang of ageing immune cells in mice.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.710
In fruit flies, one enzyme kept gut stem cells from running wild,

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:13.980
and flies with extra lived longer.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.510
Among 31,000 Americans, a first meal after noon was linked to dying sooner.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.330
And in mice,

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:28.670
a drug duo cleared tumours in all 9 and left an immune memory of the cancer.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.730
On to wellbeing. After chest-pain scares,

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.850
online therapy with a peer coach beat a referral for anxiety.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.950
And two short nights of sleep left student

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.460
s finding paintings a touch less beautiful.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.390
Now, the catch. The FDA turned down a Duchenne cell therapy again,

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:51.580
saying the evidence falls short.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.860
And UN talks on killer robots ended without binding rules; talks run to 2028.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.420
On the frontier, a battery-free sticker shifts colour with each heartbeat,

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:07.770
and a phone films it.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:11.860
Swiss physicists modelled a 40-year fusion puzzl

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.820
e: how much heating flips plasma into high gear.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.110
At McGill, bacteria in a maze chip solved small maths puzzles,

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:21.990
multiplying as they worked.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.220
Machines checked all 17 million lines.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:28.650
Understanding it is our job now. It checks out!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.510
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.710
Somehow, the future keeps landing early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.350
That's one day of news. Imagine what a year looks like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.170
You've been watching the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.330
Stay well. Same time tomorrow?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
